1. First Visit to the Website
The user opens the CopyMyLife website → sees the home page → reads about the site's concept:
routines, habits, and progress → explores popular routines → can go to Explore or sign up.
2. Sign Up
The user clicks `Sign up` → enters their full name, email, and password → clicks `Create
account` → the account is created → the user is taken to the home page as a logged-in user →
the user's name appears in the header.
3. Sign In
The user clicks `Sign in` → enters their email and password → clicks `Sign in` → if the credentials
are correct, the user is taken to the home page → if they are incorrect, an error message should
appear.
4. Explore Routines
The user opens `Explore` → sees a list of public routines → can search by title, person, or
keywords → can filter by category: All, Morning, Fitness, Study, Wellness, Productivity, Creators
→ selects an interesting routine → clicks `View routine`.
5. View a Routine Page
The user opens a specific routine page → sees the title, author, description, category, duration,
number of habits, rating, saves, likes, and comments → reviews the list of habits in the routine →
can save, like, rate, comment on, or start the routine.
6. Save Routine
The user clicks `Save` / `Saved` → the routine is saved to their profile → the save count
increases → the routine appears in the `Saved Routines` section.
7. Like Routine
The user clicks the Like button → the button becomes highlighted → the like count increases →
the routine appears in the `Liked Routines` section.
8. Rating
The user selects a number of stars → the rating is saved → the routine's overall rating is updated
→ the number of ratings increases.
9. Comments
The user types a comment in the comment field → the `Post` button becomes active → the user
clicks `Post` → the comment appears below the routine → the comment count increases → the
routine appears in the `Commented Routines` section.
10. Reply to a Comment
The user clicks `Reply` under a comment → a reply field appears → the user writes a reply →
submits it → the reply is displayed under the original comment.
11. Go to Profile
The user opens the profile menu in the header → clicks `Profile` → goes to `My Account` → sees
their avatar, name, username, bio, Edit Profile option, and side menu: Calendar, My Routines, My
Habits, Progress.
12. Edit Profile
The user clicks `Edit profile` → an editing form opens → changes their name, username, bio, or
avatar → saves the changes → the updated information appears in the profile and header.
13. My Routines
The user opens `My Routines` → sees the routines they created → can search, sort, open, edit, or
delete a routine → can also switch between Created, Saved, Liked, and Commented routines.
14. Create Routine
The user clicks `Create routine` → a form opens → enters a title, description, category, and
duration → provides an image URL or uploads an image → chooses public or private visibility →
clicks `Create routine` → the routine appears in `My Routines` → if it is public, it may appear in
Explore.
15. View Own Routine
The user opens a routine they created → sees its routine page → can review the description,
habits, comments, saves, likes, and rating → can use it like any other routine.
16. My Habits
The user opens `My Habits` → sees the habits they created → can search, sort, and view saved
habits → can create a new habit.
17. Create Habit
The user clicks `Create habit` → enters a habit name and description → selects a routine and
duration → clicks `Create habit` → the habit appears in `My Habits` → it also appears within the
selected routine.
18. Calendar
The user opens `Calendar` → sees a weekly calendar → selects a routine → chooses a day →
chooses a time → selects a repeat option: Doesn't repeat / Every day / Every week → clicks `Add
to calendar` → the routine appears in the calendar at the chosen day and time.
19. Start Routine
The user opens a routine → clicks `Start routine` → begins performing the routine → works
through the habits in order → marks each habit as completed → after all habits are finished, the
routine is considered completed.
20. Complete Routine
The user finishes all habits → a routine completion state or `Routine completed` modal appears
→ the user can click Continue / View details / Edit, depending on the design → the completed
routine is recorded in progress.
21. Progress
The user opens `Progress` → selects Day / Week / Month / Year → sees progress for routines and
habits → sees completed routines, completed habits, categories, and completion percentages.
22. Saved / Liked / Commented Sections
The user returns to their profile → opens Saved Routines, Liked Routines, or Commented
Routines → sees all the routines they have interacted with → can open any of them again.
23. Log Out
The user opens the profile menu → clicks `Log Out` → signs out of the account → the header
shows `Sign in` and `Sign up` again
